# Drafted by Gemini (R17 ending), edited.

~ farewell
if not flag.mr_farewell_done
set mr_farewell_done
set act2_done += 1
# Act II raises the party four levels, 4 to 8, whichever chapters they are (plan 5.1): the fifth chapter done gives none.
if flag.act2_done <= 4
xp milestone
endif
cutscene mr_home
cutscene mr_home_2
cutscene end
endif
Narrator: Rain patters on four warped skiffs moored beside your boat, enough timber to carry thirty souls across the dark water. Without her serum, Nurse Godlee slips away with her masked orderlies, already whispering of some new ward.
* [if flag.lethic_antidote_doses >= 1] Decide who receives the antidote -> memorys_rest/workbench:triage
* [ends:the_lethic_antidote if quest.the_lethic_antidote == learned] Row home, with Catherine and the patients -> farewell_go
* [ends:amos_cousin] [ends:the_lethic_antidote if quest.the_lethic_antidote == learned] Row home without Catherine -> farewell_leave

~ farewell_go
Narrator: Oars bite the grey lake water, and the rescued patients sit huddled in damp wool, watching the red brick island shrink into mist.
if not flag.godlee_fate
set godlee_fate = "fled"
endif
set amos_cousin_saved
set mr_patients_saved += 12
if quest.the_lethic_antidote == learned
quest the_lethic_antidote lost
endif
move wickermoor_village
-> END

~ farewell_leave
Narrator: The oars bite the grey water, and one seat in the stern stays empty. Behind you the isle keeps its violet windows, and somewhere in them a woman holds her left arm.
if not flag.godlee_fate
set godlee_fate = "fled"
endif
set mr_patients_saved += 11
quest amos_cousin left
if quest.the_lethic_antidote == learned
quest the_lethic_antidote lost
endif
move wickermoor_village
-> END

~ amos_reward
set mr_paid
gold +50
if flag.amos_cousin_cured
catherine_winthrop [weary]: I know the smell of wet hay and our old porch, though this left arm still feels borrowed from a stranger. You gave me back my name.
amos_dority [smile]: She knows me, and she knows the farm, even if the island left its mark on her. The village families pooled fifty gold pieces for the folk you brought home.
quest amos_cousin home_cured
endif
if not flag.amos_cousin_cured
if flag.amos_cousin_saved
catherine_winthrop [smile]: The lanterns here are very pretty, though not so quiet as the Matron's parlour. Who is this kind man holding my sleeve?
amos_dority [sad]: She breathes at my hearth again, even if she looks right through me like a stranger on the road. Take this fifty gold from the village kin for bringing our people back.
quest amos_cousin home_hollow
endif
if not flag.amos_cousin_saved
amos_dority [sad]: Empty boat seat where Catherine ought to be, and I will have to tell her mother the lake kept her. Still, the other families raised fifty gold for the souls you did save.
quest amos_cousin left
endif
endif
quest all_is_well back_in_wickermoor
-> END

~ mayor_amulet
wendel_somerton [smile]: Word has reached the Council that you broke that dreadful sanatorium's hold and recovered a working remedy. Sign this receipt in triplicate, and take this emerald oak leaf, our parish's heirloom Amulet of Health.
give amulet_of_health
set mayor_amulet_given
-> END

~ morgan_slow_cure
morgan [smile]: With these ward diagrams and a slow copper kettle, I can distil a gentler draught, one dose every eight hours... Nobody left blank by that island will stay forgotten for long.
set mr_morgan_cure
-> END
